message: "If you reference this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Zeno: an open-source ticketing platform with tested correctness guarantees"
abstract: >-
  Zeno is an open-source ticketing platform. It takes an event from an organizer's
  draft through a public catalog, a 15-minute inventory hold, a confirmation that
  issues one independently scannable ticket per seat, and an atomic admission at
  the door. Its distinguishing property is that correctness under a flash sale is
  asserted by tests rather than assumed: inventory cannot be oversold, a retried
  confirmation cannot create a second order, and two scanners racing on one
  credential produce one admission. It ships the operational surface as well,
  including Prometheus metrics, provisioned dashboards, alert rules, and a
  reproducible secret scan.
type: software
authors:
